---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **무엇이 덜 읽히나, 그리고 그게 한국 일인가.** (`/what-kind-fell`)
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **못 쓰는 갈래를 감추지 않는다.** 셋 중 둘을 못 썼다. 빼면 「한국만 떨어졌다」로 읽힌다.
 *    ⭐ 그래서 **못 쓴 갈래에도 수를 보인다** — 다만 「이 수로는 말할 수 없다」를 붙여서.
 * ⛔ **「일본에 졌다」로 안 쓴다.** 일본은 대조군이지 경쟁자가 아니다.
 * ⛔ **하나빼기를 한쪽으로만 읽는다.** 잡은 흔들림은 진짜, 못 잡은 것은 **모르는 것**이다.
 * ⛔ **갈래는 우리가 나눈 것**이라고 지면에 적는다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 *
 * 🔴 Astro 앞말(`---` 사이)은 **TypeScript 다.** JSX 를 넣으면 빌드가 죽는다.
 * 🔴 앞말에서 `export function` 을 쓰지 않는다 — Astro 가 딴 스코프로 옮긴다.
 * 🔴 JSX 는 끝 공백을 버린다. 붙여 써야 할 곳은 `{' '}` 를 넣는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import KcwCardnews from '../../components/KcwCardnews.astro';
import KcwShorts from '../../components/KcwShorts.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-what-kind-fell.json';

const 쓸것 = d.usable[0];
const 몫 = (v: number) => `${v > 0 ? '+' : '−'}${Math.abs(v).toFixed(1)}%`;

const TITLE = 'Southeast Asia is reading less about Korean language and craft — '
  + 'and less about Japan\'s too';
const DESC =
  `Reads of Korean language, Hangul, hanbok and taekwondo fell ${Math.abs(쓸것.korea.medianChangePc)}% `
  + `across four Southeast Asian Wikipedias. The Japanese equivalents fell `
  + `${Math.abs(쓸것.japan.medianChangePc)}%. Two other genres we measured could not be used at all.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: d.window,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/what-kind-fell">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    Of the three genres we measured, only one survived the check we run before publishing a
    median. In that one — language, writing, dress and martial art — Korean articles fell
    {' '}{Math.abs(쓸것.korea.medianChangePc)}% and the Japanese articles beside them fell
    {' '}{Math.abs(쓸것.japan.medianChangePc)}%. Both fell. That points away from Korea, not at it.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The genre we can report</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Reads per million reads of each Wikipedia, summed across
      {' '}{d.editions.map((e) => d.editionNames[e]).join(', ')}. The window is {d.window} — the
      first twelve months against the last twelve.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Article</th><th>First 12 months</th><th>Last 12 months</th><th>Change</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {쓸것.korea.articles.map((a) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{a.title}</td>
              <td class="fine">{a.before}</td>
              <td class="fine">{a.after}</td>
              <td>{몫(a.changePc)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          <tr class="ctrl"><td colspan="4" class="fine">Control — the same kind of article about Japan</td></tr>
          {쓸것.japan.articles.map((a) => (
            <tr class="ctrl">
              <td class="nm">{a.title}</td>
              <td class="fine">{a.before}</td>
              <td class="fine">{a.after}</td>
              <td>{몫(a.changePc)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      The Japanese articles are here as a control, not as a competitor. If they had held steady
      while the Korean ones fell, the fall would be about Korea. They did not. Both sides of the
      table are down by roughly the same amount, which means what moved is the appetite for this
      kind of article — the reference kind, the kind you open to learn what something is.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The two we could not use</h2>
    <p>
      We measured three genres. Two of them produced numbers that look like a finding and are not
      one. Here they are anyway, because leaving them out would turn this page into a claim it
      cannot support.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Genre</th><th>Korea</th><th>Japan (control)</th><th>Why we cannot use it</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.notUsable.map((g) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{g.name}</td>
              <td>{몫(g.korea.medianChangePc)} <span class="fine">({g.korea.measured} articles)</span></td>
              <td>{몫(g.japan.medianChangePc)} <span class="fine">({g.japan.measured} articles)</span></td>
              <td class="fine">
                Removing one article moves the {g.swingIn.join(' and ')} figure by more than half
                its own size
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="warn">
      ⚠ <strong>Read those two rows as unmeasured, not as a result.</strong> Korean music at
      {' '}{몫(d.notUsable[0].korea.medianChangePc)} against Japanese music at
      {' '}{몫(d.notUsable[0].japan.medianChangePc)} is the kind of gap that would make a headline.
      It rests on four articles and three, and taking one out of either moves the answer far
      enough to reverse it. We are not going to print it as though it held.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we decided what we could use</h2>
    <p>
      Each genre here holds three to five articles, so every figure on this page is the median of
      a handful. Before publishing any median we remove one observation, recompute, and repeat for
      each — a jackknife. If that moves the answer by more than half its own size, we do not
      report it.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      ⚠ The check runs in one direction only. A jackknife understates how much a median varies and
      is not consistent for the median, so a swing it finds is real while a swing it misses may
      simply be one it cannot see. Language and craft passing the check is not proof that its
      figure is solid — it is the absence of one specific way of being fragile. The
      {' '}<a href="/one-out">method and its limits are here</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What this page cannot tell you</h2>
    {d.cannotSay.map((s) => <p class="note">{s}</p>)}
    <p class="note">⚠ {d.genresAreOurs}</p>
    <p class="note">
      Reads — Wikimedia Pageviews API, human traffic only, monthly. The most recent month is
      dropped because Wikimedia's monthly totals can still be filling when we fetch.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwCardnews set="shelf" count={5} />

  <KcwShorts set="shelf"
    says={`A man and a woman read out the two medians side by side — the Korean articles and `
      + `the Japanese ones beside them — and say plainly that both fell.`} />

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/what-kind-fell" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  .warn { border-left: 3px solid #b45309; padding-left: 1rem; }
  .ctrl { opacity: 0.72; }
</style>
